@startuml selftest-flip
' UML activity diagram only: actions, decisions, partitions and notes, and no
' other diagram or UML element type. The same probe, once without a jail and
' once with one.
' Source of record for docs/diagrams/selftest-flip.svg. Do not edit the SVG:
' render it with the pinned PlantUML image (docs/adopting.md).
title selftest: the same probe, once without a jail and once with one

|baseline executor|
start
:run agentjail __probe as a plain host process\n(no podman, no jail);
if (the hazard happens on the host?) then (yes)
  :EXPECTED: the negative is real;
else (no)
  :FAIL: the assertion is vacuous;
endif
stop

|jailed executor|
start
:stage the same binary read-only into the jail,\na generated class (address_policy=lan), a fixture target;
:run agentjail __probe inside the jail;
if (the negative is denied?) then (yes)
  :PASS;
else (no)
  :FAIL: names the case that escaped;
endif
:positive control: one granted destination answers\nthrough the gateway and its audit line is read back;
if (answered and audited?) then (yes)
  :PASS;
else (no)
  :FAIL;
endif
stop

legend right
  A case that cannot run in baseline prints SKIPPED-BASELINE with the reason,
  never silently omitted. Baseline exit 0 plus jailed exit 0 means every hazard
  is real and every hazard is denied.
endlegend
@enduml
